This directory vendors, with modifications, source from NVLabs' alpamayo1.5 repository:

    https://github.com/NVlabs/alpamayo1.5
    commit 36aeb4c (2026-09-09)
    Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory)

Files, and their origin under the upstream repo's `src/alpamayo1_5/`:

    rotation.py                  <- geometry/rotation.py
    action_space.py               <- action_space/action_space.py
    action_space_utils.py         <- action_space/utils.py
    unicycle_accel_curvature.py   <- action_space/unicycle_accel_curvature.py

Modifications from the upstream source (every change is a dependency removal, not a behavior
change -- verified bit-exact against upstream, see
test/unit/test_alpamayo_action_space.py):

* Internal imports rewritten from the `alpamayo1_5.*` package path to relative imports within this
  `_vendor` package (these files are not installed as part of `alpamayo1_5`; they are copied here
  so the Neuron plugin has no runtime dependency on that package, which pins Python 3.12 and needs
  hydra/scipy -- see the model package's `config.py`).
* `rotation.py`: `scipy.spatial.transform.Rotation` is now imported lazily inside `euler_2_so3`
  (a numpy helper not used by any inference path in this plugin) instead of at module level, so
  importing this module does not require scipy.
* `action_space_utils.py`: six `einops.einsum("... i j, ... i k -> ... j k")` /
  `einops.einsum("... i j, ... i -> ... j")` calls (least-squares normal-equation assembly in
  `construct_DTD`, `dxy_theta_to_v_without_v0`, `dxy_theta_to_v`, `theta_smooth`) rewritten as the
  equivalent explicit `.transpose(-1, -2) @ ...` batched matmuls, removing the `einops` dependency
  (not available in the shared Neuron venv; a package request was not filed since the rewrite is
  a direct, verified-equivalent substitution, not a new capability).

Everything else is byte-for-byte identical to the upstream source, including comments and
docstrings.
